    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's what was happening:\n\n**The Problem:** JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic converts decimal prices to cents imprecisely. When `parseEuros` multiplied 39.95 by 100, it got 3995.0000000000005 instead of the whole number 3995, causing the validation to reject it.\n\n**The Fix:** I added `Math.round()` to both `parseEuros` (line 13) and `cellCents` (line 25) in `src/money.js` to ensure the multiplication result is properly rounded to a whole number.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 50 existing tests still pass \u2713\n- Can now add Gym at \u20ac39.95 \u2713  \n- Netflix (\u20ac12.99) and Spotify (\u20ac10.99) still work \u2713\n- Data is correctly saved and displayed \u2713",
